@casperisfine it seems that this change the default behavior of
`ActiveSupport::Cache::Store.retrieve_pool_options`
and causes [ActiveSupport::Cache::RedisCacheStore#initialize](https://github.com/rails/rails/blob/600a052c8cf6d355bd2d3f867cecce7cefdb1894/activesupport/lib/active_support/cache/redis_cache_store.rb#L148-L152) to use a `::ConnectionPool ` when it did not before
 
```ruby
if pool_options = self.class.send(:retrieve_pool_options, redis_options)
  @redis = ::ConnectionPool.new(pool_options) { self.class.build_redis(**redis_options) }
else
  @redis = self.class.build_redis(**redis_options)
end
```  

WDYT?
